translated_content:
It was interesting to see a mahogany forest.
And the free-roaming monkeys were quite interesting too.
But if you&#39;ve already been somewhere else in the rainforest, you&#39;d say, &quot;Yeah, this is quite nice.&quot;

posted_on:
A huge thank you to Bilal for this rich and intense cultural immersion. Bilal is an incredibly kind young man, driven by a desire to share the &quot;real&quot; life of Zanzibar and the culture of fruits and spices with as many people as possible.
We spent nearly three hours with him, first in the village and then at the plantation, and he perfectly adapted to our pace (my wife, our two young children, ages 7 and 9), and answered all our questions.
We particularly appreciated the authenticity of this visit...and that of Bilal himself, who, as he told us several times, &quot;had dreamed of becoming a guide in his village since he was a little boy.&quot;
